<title>ITALY: Bank Italy's Fazio urges structural spending cuts.</title>
<headline>Bank Italy's Fazio urges structural spending cuts.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Italy governor Antonio Fazio said on Thursday that Italy would enjoy bigger-than-expected interest rate falls if the government introduced structural spending changes.</p>
<p>Fazio told a parliamentary commission that recent government spending targets contained in the three-year programme of economic forecasts (DPEF) appeared &quot;excessive&quot;.</p>
</text>
